  "method": "Independently authored scalar kernels; optional deref pair compares mutable scalar references with C pointer writes; optional vector_slot pair compares checked one-element Vec<u32>.at_mut with a checked C vector slot. Same stdin input and QPC/output support. All workloads guard seed<65521 and rounds<=50000000; arithmetic is proven in-range over admitted inputs. Fairy retains ordinary checked arithmetic and full required product support; C does not link Fairy support. 5 alternating paired samples after one build/run warmup per workload/lane. Kernel time excludes input parsing, process startup and printing; result is consumed and independently checked in Go. Build time covers source read/load, frontend analysis/verified MIR, C emission, C compile/link, artifact reads and final EXE write; common warmed toolchain discovery, harness process startup, workspace setup and execution excluded. No persistent package cache; ambient OS caches uncontrolled. No PDB, runtime-speed generalization, Linux, real parser/container workload or cold CLI startup claim.",
